     "en": "A short story"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Raju's class made a chart showing who makes laws, who carries them out and who settles disputes.\n\"Power is shared,\" said the teacher."
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "legislature",
     "executive",
     "judiciary"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Government has three organs. The legislature makes laws, the executive carries them out and the judiciary settles disputes and checks that laws are followed.\nSeparation of powers stops any one organ from becoming too strong.\nThere are three levels: central (Union), state and local governments. Panchayats and municipalities are local."
    }
